  "Stations are the setup's (not moved); the scene is the Stage 2 scene.xml unchanged (box re-placed in Stage 2 after the camera re-registration).",
  "Strategy (differs from the human's two-hand edge pinch, see the deviations on #1.2 and #2.1): #1 the right middle fingertip holds the tray's back down; the left index, curled under the lid's left edge 7 cm from the hinge, turns the lid with the hand (rigid follow) from lying open (189 deg) to upright (96 deg); the right hand lets go of the tray and returns home while the left fingertip holds the upright lid. #2 the left fingertip tips the lid 14 deg past upright; it swings shut onto the box (caught briefly on the left thumb at 46 deg) and the left middle fingertip comes down on the shut lid. #3 the right middle fingertip joins the press, then both lift off; #4 both hands withdraw home together (one two-hand entry).",
  "Measured: the tray moves 0.2 mm during the lift and 13 mm / 2.3 deg when the lid swings shut onto it; the lid ends at its shut stop (0.000 rad) and stays shut after both hands lift.",
  "Stage 1 says both hands act in every subgoal; subgoals 1, 3 and 4 have both hands acting at once (tray hold + lift; the two presses, then both lift off; one two-hand entry withdrawing both hands together); subgoal 2 is one hand (declared sequential deviation).",
  "Library issue found: SubgoalPlanner.__init__ (tool_library/common/subgoal.py) attaches every body in state['held'] through its root's free joint, so after a 'hold' or a 'close_joint' (keep_hold) on a hinged part (the lid), the next entry of that hand carries the whole box with the wrist (the dry run swung the hand 4x the lid angle and moved the box root); worked around with keep_hold false and by not using 'hold' on the lid.",
